  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">RWANDA - Capital Market Development (R-CAMD) Project</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="FR">RWANDA - REP- Projet de d&#xE9;veloppement des march&#xE9;s des capitaux du Rwanda (R-CAMD)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Management  submits  this  report  and  recommendation tothe Board  of  the African Development Fund (ADF) for consideration and approval of (i) aSovereign Loan of anamount not exceeding UA 4.10million to the Republic of Rwanda for the implementation of the Rwanda Capital Market Development Project (R-CAMD); and (ii) frontloading of UA 4.10 million which will bring the total frontloading of Rwanda&#x2019;s 2025 ADF-16 PBA1to 60.8%. The planned intervention will support the deepening of Rwanda&#x2019;s capital market and modernization of Rwanda&#x2019;s financial sector in  line  with  the  Government  of  Rwanda  (GoR)&#x2019;s  Vision  2050  and  National  Strategy  for Transformation 2024-2029(NST-2) as well as the priorities under the Kigali International Financial Centre (KIFC) to transform Rwanda to an international financial Centreserving as a financial destination for investors seeking opportunities across the African continent. The R-CAMD project will contribute to accelerating the implementation of Rwanda&#x2019;s Capital Market Masterplan (CMMP) 2018-2028, the operationalization of the KIFC, the establishment of a Rwanda Capital Market Academy and an Institute of Directors (IoD) and provide targeted capacity  building on capital market regulations and operations to financial sector ecosystem in Rwanda. This project primely contributes towards climate adaptation result. As such 100% of the total approval is attributed as climate finance, out of which 5% is adaptation finance.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The R-CAMD project will support Rwanda&#x2019;s ambition to mobilize long term savings by offering alternative attractive investment options throughits capital market thereby enabling the country to further develop and diversifyits economy. The project is expected toimprove the capital market regulatory environmentin Rwanda via infrastructure development, legal and regulatory framework&#x2019;s  introduction  for  capital  market  development.  It  will  also  strengthen  corporate governancepractices in public and private sectors through the support for the Institute of Directors and provide targeted capacity building to increase the knowledge base ofthe financial market ecosystem which will increase domestic and international investors&#x2019;confidence in the market.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The direct beneficiaries of the envisaged operation are Rwanda Capital Market Authority (executing agency), Rwanda Stock Exchange, Ministry of Financeand Economic Planning, Rwanda Finance  Limited  (operators  of  Kigali  International  Financial  Centre),  East  Africa  Commodities Exchange, current and potential company officials, management executives of public and private entities, SOEs and quasi parastatals charged with governance duties. The R-CAMD project willsupport key market infrastructure and regulatory reforms to promote financial markets innovation and improve corporate governance and skills set of managers and staff of private and public sector institutions in Rwanda.</narrative>
  </description>
